   "speech and gaps": "Speech: each line from its start on the radio cut's timeline to that start plus the measured length of its file, pauses inside a line included. Gaps: the seven stretches between the end of one line and the start of the next.",
   "stems": "voice: the narration track, every line with its own gain. music: the score after its gain and fades and after the compressor keyed by the voice, with no voice in it. music_unducked: the same without the compressor. premix: voice plus music, as it goes into the last step. limited: the premix after the limiter.",
   "reduction_db": "Level of music_unducked minus level of music over the same windows: what the compressor took off the music. deepest_db is the largest value in any one 50 ms window.",
   "before_normaliser": "Levels of the stems as they go into the last step (the limiter, then loudnorm).",
   "in_final_mix": "The same in the finished mix. The last step applies one gain to voice and music together, so each 50 ms of a stem is scaled by the gain of that 50 ms: mean square of the finished mix over mean square of the premix. The finished mix is read later by the limiter's delay, so that the same sound is compared.",
   "voice_over_music_db": "Level of voice minus level of music, both over the speech spans.",
   "voice_over_music_lu": "The same in loudness units, before the last step: voice and music each cut down to the speech spans and measured with `pipeline.core.loudness` (K-weighted and gated, one decimal).",
   "music_rise_in_gaps_db": "Level of music over the gaps minus level of music over the speech spans. It holds the score's own changes too: see the two music_unducked levels.",
   "limiter": "ceiling_dbfs: the limit `loudnorm_two_pass` sets, null when it does not limit. delay_samples: how late the limiter gives its output, found by sending one click through it. The limited file is read later by that much. windows: 50 ms windows in the mix. windows_over_ceiling: windows of the premix with a sample over the ceiling. windows_touched: windows whose level the limiter lowered by 0.1 dB or more, and windows_touched_in_speech those of them inside a line. largest_peak_cut_db: the most it took off the highest sample of a window. largest_window_drop_db: the most it took off the level of a window. takes_off_speech_db: level of the premix minus level of the limited file over the speech spans. takes_off_lu: integrated loudness of the premix minus that of the limited file, both as loudnorm measures them.",
   "normaliser": "pipeline_says: what `build_mix` returns as `normalised`. second_pass_ran: the mode loudnorm itself reports for its last pass. gain_before_limiter_db and gain_after_limiter_db: target loudness minus the loudness loudnorm measured, on the premix and on the limited file. peak_after_gain_dbtp: true peak of the limited file plus the second of those gains, to hold against the true-peak target. gain_speech_db and gain_gaps_db: level of the finished mix minus level of the premix over the same windows, so the limiter is in them. gain_low_db and gain_high_db: the 5th and the 95th percentile of that gain per 50 ms window, over the windows where the premix is above -60 dBFS. loudnorm_low_db and loudnorm_high_db: the same two percentiles for loudnorm alone, finished mix over limited file.",
   "per_line": "voice_db, music_db, reduction_db and voice_over_music_db as above, over that line alone and before the last step. gain_db: the gain `build_mix` gave the line. voice_lufs: the voice stem cut down to the line, by `pipeline.core.loudness`. limiter_takes_off_db: level of the premix minus level of the limited file over the line. mix_db and mix_lufs: the finished mix over the line, voice and the music under it together, as a level and by `pipeline.core.loudness`. reduction_before_line_db: the reduction in the 50 ms before the first window of the line in which the voice is above the compressor's threshold. reduction_0_1s_in_db: the reduction in the 50 ms that start 0.1 s after that first window starts. back_within_3db_s and back_within_1db_s: the clock starts at the end of the last window of the line in which the voice is above the threshold, and stops at the start of the first window where the reduction is under 3 dB, or under 1 dB. null: the next line started first. silence_after_s: from the same start of the clock to the start of the next line, or to the end.",
   "line_spread": "Lowest, highest and highest minus lowest over the eight lines, for voice_db and for mix_lufs.",
   "per_gap": "music_db and reduction_db over that gap alone, before the last step.",
   "checks": "copy_gives_the_pipeline_mix: the copied chain gives the same finished file as the pipeline's `build_mix`, byte for byte. The run stops when it does not. premix_peak_dbfs: the highest sample of the premix. premix_samples_over_full_scale: samples of the premix at 1.0 or more, either sign. The premix is a float file, so they are kept as they are. mix_samples_at_full_scale: samples of the 16 bit finished mix at the highest or the lowest value the format has. music_ends_s: the length of the music stem as the compressor gives it out, to hold against total_s."
  },
